    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511-a1">

                <pb facs="0977" n="883" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg883"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 169.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mrs. Lay to Mr. Bell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brooklyn</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 20,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I write you if you could give me any
                    information in reference to a claim under the name of Du Boise, which is held by
                    the Government of Netherlands awaiting claimant.</p>
                <p>The reason why is that a party in New York is representing to the decedent’s
                    heirs that such is the case, and I would like to know if there is any thing in
                    it.</p>
                <p>By doing so I shall esteem it a great favor.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Catherine W. Lay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
